119153	119287	119318	119318	she	3861	" and indeed without much vanity : my life has been so simple and sequestered , I have had but few enticements to attempt such things . And what a warning , my beautiful , my noble , friend , is this melancholy state in which I see you ! Accept of me a vow , which is suited to my heart ; which , under the emotion you have caused me , has settled into words and shape , and will be hallowed by the hour in which I utter it . Each transitory inclination I will study to withstand , and even the most earnest I will keep within my bosom : no woman shall receive an acknowledgment of love from my lips to whom I can not consecrate my life ! "
